<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3335" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ărānĕus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		1. araneus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I. A..</b>
			<i>Pertaining to the spider</i>, <i>spider's-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 17, 44, § 156</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">texta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					29, 4, 27, § 86</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ărā-nĕum</span></b> ,
			i, n., <i>a spider's
			web</i>, = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀράχνιον</span>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tollere haec aranea quantum est laboris?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 2, 8, 23</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A disease of the vine and of the olive-tree</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				17, 24, 36, § 7</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Araneus mus, <i>a kind
				of small mouse</i>, acc. to some <i>the
				shrew-mouse</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 6, 17, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 8, 58,
				83, § 227</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
